      <Id>OT-R05</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Logic or configuration changes on {target.Name} cannot be proven or reconstructed</ShortTitle>
      <Category>R</Category>
      <Description>Program downloads, online edits and parameter changes made on {target.Name} by {source.Name} may not be recorded with who made them, what changed and when. After an incident it cannot be shown whether a change was authorised, accidental or malicious.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Program downloads, online edits and parameter changes made on {target.Name} by {source.Name} may not be recorded with who made them, what changed and when. After an incident it cannot be shown whether a change was authorised, accidental or malicious.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Priority</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Medium</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Priority</Description>
          <Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>PossibleMitigations</Name>
          <Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Record every logic, configuration and firmware change with user identity, timestamp and a before/after hash or version (CR 2.8). Keep a change history on the device or engineering server. Support non-repudiation for critical changes at SL 3 and above (CR 2.12). Compare running logic with the approved baseline.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Recommended controls for this threat.</Description>
          <Id>PossibleMitigations</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>SDLPhase</Name>
          <Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>SR - Security requirements</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>IEC 62443-4-1 secure development practice that addresses this threat.</Description>
          <Id>SDLPhase</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>ATTACKICS</Name>
          <Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
