      <Id>OT-R06</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Local audit trail on {target.Name} lost, overwritten or cleared</ShortTitle>
      <Category>R</Category>
      <Description>Embedded and network devices often keep only a small local event buffer. An attacker could clear it, flood it until older events are overwritten, or reboot {target.Name} so evidence held in volatile memory is lost.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Embedded and network devices often keep only a small local event buffer. An attacker could clear it, flood it until older events are overwritten, or reboot {target.Name} so evidence held in volatile memory is lost.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Priority</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Medium</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Priority</Description>
          <Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>PossibleMitigations</Name>
          <Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Protect audit records against deletion (CR 3.9) and keep them across restarts. Forward events in near real time to a central collector (CR 6.1, syslog over TLS). Warn when audit capacity is nearly used (CR 2.9). Record clearing of the log as an audit event itself.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Recommended controls for this threat.</Description>
          <Id>PossibleMitigations</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>SDLPhase</Name>
          <Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>SD - Secure by design</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>IEC 62443-4-1 secure development practice that addresses this threat.</Description>
          <Id>SDLPhase</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>ATTACKICS</Name>
          <Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>T0872 Indicator Removal on Host; T0816 Device Restart/Shutdown</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Related MITRE ATT&amp;CK for ICS technique(s), v20 IDs.</Description>
          <Id>ATTACKICS</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
