      <Id>OT-D14</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Command, trip or alarm messages between {source.Name} and {target.Name} blocked</ShortTitle>
      <Category>D</Category>
      <Description>An attacker on the path, or on a device in between, could selectively drop or delay commands, trips, alarms or status messages between {source.Name} and {target.Name} while the link still looks healthy, so a response to a process upset never arrives.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>An attacker on the path, or on a device in between, could selectively drop or delay commands, trips, alarms or status messages between {source.Name} and {target.Name} while the link still looks healthy, so a response to a process upset never arrives.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Priority</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>High</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Priority</Description>
          <Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>PossibleMitigations</Name>
          <Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Use communication watchdogs, heartbeats and sequence counters so that missing or late messages are detected (CR 3.1, CR 7.1). Define the safe state on loss of communication (CR 3.6). Alarm on communication loss to the operator. Use redundant paths for essential functions and keep safety trips independent of the control network.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Recommended controls for this threat.</Description>
          <Id>PossibleMitigations</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>SDLPhase</Name>
          <Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>SD - Secure by design</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>IEC 62443-4-1 secure development practice that addresses this threat.</Description>
          <Id>SDLPhase</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
