      <Id>OT-E22</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Attacker tools staged on {target.Name} to reach the control network</ShortTitle>
      <Category>E</Category>
      <Description>{target.Name} has network access to controllers. An attacker who gets code onto it (drive-by download, script, phishing, lateral transfer from another host) could use built-in tools, scripts or API hooking to scan, move laterally and send commands as a trusted host.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>{target.Name} has network access to controllers. An attacker who gets code onto it (drive-by download, script, phishing, lateral transfer from another host) could use built-in tools, scripts or API hooking to scan, move laterally and send commands as a trusted host.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Priority</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>High</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Priority</Description>
          <Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>PossibleMitigations</Name>
          <Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Use application allow-listing and block script interpreters that are not needed (HDR 3.2, SAR 2.4). Do not allow web browsing or e-mail on OT hosts (CR 5.3 person-to-person communication). Restrict outbound and lateral connections from the host. Monitor for new executables and tools.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Recommended controls for this threat.</Description>
          <Id>PossibleMitigations</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>SDLPhase</Name>
          <Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>SG - Security guidelines</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>IEC 62443-4-1 secure development practice that addresses this threat.</Description>
          <Id>SDLPhase</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>ATTACKICS</Name>
          <Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>T0867 Lateral Tool Transfer; T0817 Drive-by Compromise; T0874 Hooking; T1701.001 Command and Scripting Interpreter: PowerShell; T0852 Screen Capture; T0840 Network Connection Enumeration</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Related MITRE ATT&amp;CK for ICS technique(s), v20 IDs.</Description>
          <Id>ATTACKICS</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
